Definition:
     An array is a fundamental and linear data structure that stores a collection of elements of the same data type  in contiguous memory locations

Array Declaration:
     Syntax:
             Data_Type variable_Name [];   Here "[]" denotes object primitive.
                      or
             Data_Type [] variable_Name;   Here "[]" denotes object primitive.

Creating an Array:
     Data_Type variable_Name [] = new Data_Type [size of the array];
                              or
     Data_Type variable_Name [] = {_,_,_,_,_,_};

Array Initialization:
     1) Direct Method:
               Data_Type variable_Name [] = {_,_,_,_,_,_};
     2) Using Scanner Class:
               Data_Type variable_Name [] = new Data_Type [size of the array];
